{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1553742-cwod-transformers-beast-wars","id":1553742,"title":"[cWoD]Transformers: Beast Wars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-09-10T21:09:57-07:00","id":1553742,"title":"[cWoD]Transformers: Beast Wars","content":"Has anyone ever heard of this fansplat made by Amanda Flowers, before? <br /> <br /> This fansplat was probably the most high effort fansplat I have ever read by far! It's just so great and full of immense detail. You can tell that the person who made it was connoisseur of how cWoD mechanics ran, along with having a great mind toward making up homebrew to play robotic characters (who happen to take up animal forms, no less lol). It's just so simplistic and complex, that I loved reading every part of this fansplat. (Also, near to the end of the chapter material for the fansplat, I think I remember that they provided supplementary rules for playing Cybertronians in the normal greater cWoD-verse; which I found to be absolutely amazing. <br /> <br /> I knew about this RPG for years myself, but now I wonder (if the few remaining, if any) cWoD fans knew about this fansplat themselves as well. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, on another note, it seems the author shut down the site from which Transformers: Beast Wars rpg was hosted; most likely the maintenance for it failed to be feasible for a time, but still admirable for how long they kept it up regardless from 2001 to 2023.. 22 years.. JEEZ.<br /> <br /> It can still be accessed via wayback however and someone else has made a PDF 2nd edition version of the game themselves. I haven't gotten the chance to read it myself due to being busy, but I skimmed through some material, and I liked it thus far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-24T07:26:44-07:00","id":1553992,"title":"","content":"I had not. I do remember the Highlander treatment someone made from around that time, though I can't speak to how well its mechanics were handled.<br /> <br /> Did it handle the various generations of Beast Wars characters (e.g. original, transmetal, fuzor, etc.)? Also did it limit itself to the show or also incorporate ideas from the toy line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}